{number: 97}
{title: It is Well with My Soul}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
When [C] peace like a river at-[F] tendeth my [C] way,
When [Am] sorrows like [D7] sea billows [G7] roll;
What-[C] ever my [F] lot, Thou hast [D7] taught me to [G7] say,
It is [C] well, it is [F] well [G7] with my [C] soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
It is [C] well with my [G7] soul,
It is [C] well, it is [F] well [G7] with my [C] soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Though [C] Satan should buffet, though [F] trials should [C] come,
Let [Am] this blest as-[D7] surance con-[G7] trol,
That [C] Christ has re-[F] garded my [D7] helpless es-[G7] tate,
And hath [C] shed His own [F] blood [G7] for my [C] soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
My [C] sin, oh, the bliss of this [F] glorious [C] thought!
My [Am] sin, not in [D7] part but the [G7] whole,
Is [C] nailed to the [F] cross, and I [D7] bear it no [G7] more,
Praise the [C] Lord, praise the [F] Lord, [G7] O my [C] soul!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [C] Lord, haste the day when my [F] faith shall be [C] sight,
The [Am] clouds be rolled [D7] back as a [G7] scroll;
The [C] trump shall re-[F] sound, and the [D7] Lord shall de-[G7] scend,
Even [C] so, it is [F] well [G7] with my [C] soul.
{end_of_verse}
